      "message": "fix(post): Tormach writes no motion for a refused first traverse\n\nA first X/Y traverse with no ClearancePlane or RetractPlane was refused\nby name, but the move itself was still written as one combined rapid\nfrom an unknown height. xyFirst and startXY now return false on the\nrefusal; each caller (rapid, feed, arc, probe guard, probe move, canned\ncycle) then writes nothing, as #1636 does for the Fanuc family. The\nrefusal pin asserts no X/Y word reaches the text.\n\nAlso: restore main's tester-kit .camproj (the WRITE_GOLDEN re-save of\nmicroarc_test_part changed only its format, not the kit); add the\n\"Taken on trust\" record to the decision file; state the no-motion rule\nin assets/posts/AGENTS.md.\n\nFixes #1614\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
